WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.270
Eva spent the first week of high school trying to keep her head above water.
上高中的第一周，伊娃一直在拼命应付，才勉强没有掉队。

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.140
One of the major headaches for her was finding her way in the huge school building.
让她头疼的大事之一，就是在这栋巨大的教学楼里找路。

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.380
It was a six-story building.
这是一栋六层的楼。

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:20.010
On each floor, hallways stretched in four directions, leading to classrooms, laboratories, and teachers’ offices.
每层楼都有走廊向四个方向延伸，通往教室、实验室和老师的办公室。

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:25.230
Somewhere in the building, there was also a library, a cafeteria, and a gym.
楼里的某个地方还有图书馆、食堂和体育馆。

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:31.400
Having a poor sense of direction, Eva found it impossible to get around in such a huge building.
伊娃方向感很差，觉得在这么大的楼里根本没法四处走动。

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.210
All the different hallways and rooms were too much to think about, let alone commit to memory.
这么多不同的走廊和房间，光是想想就让她头大，更别说记住了。

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:43.900
She decided that she would memorize where her classes were and then pretend that the rest of the place didn’t exist.
她决定把上课的教室位置记下来，然后当这栋楼的其他地方都不存在。

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.970
In her first PE class, Eva was shocked when Coach Pitt announced that everyone had to run one mile around the track outside.
第一节体育课上，皮特教练宣布每个人都要绕着外面的跑道跑一英里，伊娃吓了一跳。

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.880
She searched the faces of her classmates for signs of panic.
她在同学们的脸上搜寻惊慌的神色。

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.630
There was nothing she feared more than having to run a whole mile.
她最怕的莫过于跑整整一英里了。

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.780
To Eva, “a mile” was used to describe long distances.
在伊娃看来，“一英里”是用来形容遥远距离的。

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:10.660
It was ten miles from her home to her grandfather’s, and that always seemed like a long way, even in a car!
从她家到爷爷家有十英里，那段路总让人觉得很远，即便是坐车也一样！

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.430
When Coach Pitt blew his whistle, Eva figured she would be left in the dust.
皮特教练吹响哨子时，伊娃心想自己肯定会被远远甩在后面。

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:20.650
However, while some of her classmates edged ahead, others actually fell behind.
然而，有些同学一点点跑到了前面，另一些反倒落在了后面。

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.060
“It’s just the beginning,” she thought.
“这才刚开始呢。”她心想。

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.210
“I’ll come in last for sure.”
“我肯定会跑最后一名。”

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:30.120
Soon Eva began to breathe hard, with her heart pounding and legs shaking.
很快，伊娃开始大口喘气，心怦怦直跳，双腿发抖。

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.690
Feeling desperate, Eva started using a mind trick on herself.
绝望之中，伊娃开始对自己用一个心理小技巧。

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.410
She stopped thinking about the word “mile.”
她不再去想“英里”这个词。

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:43.030
Instead, she focused on reaching the shadow cast on the track by an oak tree up ahead.
而是把注意力集中在跑到前方一棵橡树投在跑道上的树影那里。

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:47.360
Then she concentrated on jogging to the spot where the track curved.
接着，她一心想着慢跑到跑道拐弯的地方。

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.860
After that, she tried to see if she could complete her first lap.
之后，她试着看看自己能不能跑完第一圈。

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:56.260
One lap turned into two, then three, then four.
一圈变成了两圈，接着是三圈，然后是四圈。

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.590
When Coach Pitt said “Nice work!” to her at the finish line, Eva was surprised.
皮特教练在终点线对她说“干得好！”时，伊娃很惊讶。

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.730
Eva decided to use the same trick to deal with the school building.
伊娃决定用同样的技巧来对付那栋教学楼。
